{"legit": true, "title": "Why Is the Sea Salty? Fox, Bruno and Hugo Explain", "description": "A French fox, a German bear and an Italian owl chat about why the ocean tastes of salt. Fox speaks French, Bruno speaks German and Hugo speaks Italian.", "mood": "bright", "theme": "sunrise", "language": "en", "voices": {"fox": "Ambre", "bear": "Lennart", "owl": "Lorenzo"}, "beats": [{"id": "b4796096", "narration": "Bonjour les amis ! Aujourd'hui, une grande question : pourquoi l'eau de la mer est-elle sal\u00e9e, alors que l'eau de la pluie ne l'est pas ?", "scene": {"type": "presenter", "props": {"character": "fox", "side": "left", "framing": "auto", "heading": "Pourquoi la mer est sal\u00e9e ?", "backdrop": "tall_lighthouse_cliff", "cast": ["fox", "bear", "owl"]}}, "speaker": "fox", "translation": "Hello friends! Today, a big question: why is sea water salty, when rain water is not?", "media": {"tts_hash": "a517f5e877fa019d", "audio_key": "generation/v2/d83940b7-7327-4e94-8ed9-b64f2d40f63b/audio/a517f5e877fa019d.wav", "duration": 6.287, "voice": "Ambre", "register": {"hz": 226.4, "ref": 223.8, "takes": 1}, "words_key": "generation/v2/d83940b7-7327-4e94-8ed9-b64f2d40f63b/audio/a517f5e877fa019d.words.json", "element": {}}}, {"id": "dbe0b279", "narration": "Gute Frage, Fox! Der Ozean bedeckt etwa 71 Prozent der Erde. Das ist riesig, und darin ist Salz gel\u00f6st.", "scene": {"type": "presenter", "props": {"character": "bear", "side": "left", "framing": "auto", "heading": "Der Ozean", "chart": {"labels": ["Meer", "Land"], "values": [70.8, 29.2], "unit": "%"}, "backdrop": "tall_lighthouse_cliff", "cast": ["fox", "bear", "owl"]}}, "speaker": "bear", "translation": "Good question, Fox! The ocean covers about 71 percent of the Earth. That is huge, and salt is dissolved in it.", "media": {"tts_hash": "0a3c2480bc94201f", "audio_key": "generation/v2/d83940b7-7327-4e94-8ed9-b64f2d40f63b/audio/0a3c2480bc94201f.wav", "duration": 6.643, "voice": "Lennart", "register": {"hz": 116.8, "ref": 109.3, "first_hz": 123.4, "takes": 2}, "words_key": "generation/v2/d83940b7-7327-4e94-8ed9-b64f2d40f63b/audio/0a3c2480bc94201f.words.json", "element": {}}}, {"id": "dc13ceba", "narration": "Esatto, Bruno! Il sale \u00e8 sciolto nell'acqua, come lo zucchero nel t\u00e8. Si chiama salinit\u00e0.", "scene": {"type": "presenter", "props": {"character": "owl", "side": "left", "framing": "auto", "heading": "La salinit\u00e0", "points": ["Sale sciolto nell'acqua", "Grammi per litro"], "backdrop": "tall_lighthouse_cliff", "cast": ["fox", "bear", "owl"]}}, "speaker": "owl", "translation": "Exactly, Bruno! The salt is dissolved in the water, like sugar in tea. It is called salinity.", "media": {"tts_hash": "a38ead1411a5f3c7", "audio_key": "generation/v2/d83940b7-7327-4e94-8ed9-b64f2d40f63b/audio/a38ead1411a5f3c7.wav", "duration": 5.541, "voice": "Lorenzo", "register": {"hz": 134.8, "ref": 109.6, "first_hz": 158.9, "takes": 3}, "words_key": "generation/v2/d83940b7-7327-4e94-8ed9-b64f2d40f63b/audio/a38ead1411a5f3c7.words.json", "element": {}}}, {"id": "ae8822bb", "narration": "Mais d'o\u00f9 vient ce sel, Bruno ? Est-ce que quelqu'un le verse dans la mer, comme dans une soupe ?", "scene": {"type": "presenter", "props": {"character": "fox", "side": "left", "framing": "auto", "heading": "D'o\u00f9 vient le sel ?", "backdrop": "tall_lighthouse_cliff", "cast": ["fox", "bear", "owl"]}}, "speaker": "fox", "translation": "But where does this salt come from, Bruno? Does someone pour it into the sea, like into a soup?", "media": {"tts_hash": "bdf030e1e8888f6c", "audio_key": "generation/v2/d83940b7-7327-4e94-8ed9-b64f2d40f63b/audio/bdf030e1e8888f6c.wav", "duration": 3.991, "voice": "Ambre", "register": {"hz": 221.2, "ref": 223.8, "takes": 1}, "words_key": "generation/v2/d83940b7-7327-4e94-8ed9-b64f2d40f63b/audio/bdf030e1e8888f6c.words.json", "element": {}}}, {"id": "b63115e5", "narration": "Nein, Fox! Regen l\u00f6st Salze aus Gestein. Fl\u00fcsse tragen sie ins Meer, und dort bleiben sie.", "scene": {"type": "presenter", "props": {"character": "bear", "side": "left", "framing": "auto", "heading": "Regen, Fluss, Meer", "points": ["Regen l\u00f6st Salz", "Fluss tr\u00e4gt es", "Meer sammelt es"], "backdrop": "tall_lighthouse_cliff", "cast": ["fox", "bear", "owl"]}}, "speaker": "bear", "translation": "No, Fox! Rain dissolves salts from rock. Rivers carry them to the sea, and there they stay.", "media": {"tts_hash": "a28b4157b0b1e94d", "audio_key": "generation/v2/d83940b7-7327-4e94-8ed9-b64f2d40f63b/audio/a28b4157b0b1e94d.wav", "duration": 6.207, "voice": "Lennart", "register": {"hz": 128.3, "ref": 109.3, "first_hz": 132.6, "takes": 3}, "words_key": "generation/v2/d83940b7-7327-4e94-8ed9-b64f2d40f63b/audio/a28b4157b0b1e94d.words.json", "element": {}}}, {"id": "7dbe7150", "narration": "Il sole fa evaporare l'acqua, ma il sale resta. Cos\u00ec il mare, col tempo, diventa sempre pi\u00f9 salato.", "scene": {"type": "presenter", "props": {"character": "owl", "side": "left", "framing": "auto", "heading": "Il sole e il sale", "points": ["L'acqua evapora", "Il sale resta"], "backdrop": "tall_lighthouse_cliff", "cast": ["fox", "bear", "owl"]}}, "speaker": "owl", "translation": "The sun makes the water evaporate, but the salt stays. So the sea, over time, becomes saltier and saltier.", "media": {"tts_hash": "de106e770d13759e", "audio_key": "generation/v2/d83940b7-7327-4e94-8ed9-b64f2d40f63b/audio/de106e770d13759e.wav", "duration": 6.744, "voice": "Lorenzo", "register": {"hz": 109.6, "ref": 109.6, "takes": 1}, "words_key": "generation/v2/d83940b7-7327-4e94-8ed9-b64f2d40f63b/audio/de106e770d13759e.words.json", "element": {}}}, {"id": "980dca66", "narration": "Ah, je comprends ! Le sel voyage des roches jusqu'\u00e0 la mer, et l'eau de pluie repart en nuages.", "scene": {"type": "presenter", "props": {"character": "fox", "side": "left", "framing": "auto", "heading": "Des roches \u00e0 la mer", "backdrop": "tall_lighthouse_cliff", "cast": ["fox", "bear", "owl"]}}, "speaker": "fox", "translation": "Ah, I understand! The salt travels from the rocks to the sea, and the rain water goes back up as clouds.", "media": {"tts_hash": "d917c7e8441dbf81", "audio_key": "generation/v2/d83940b7-7327-4e94-8ed9-b64f2d40f63b/audio/d917c7e8441dbf81.wav", "duration": 4.845, "voice": "Ambre", "register": {"hz": 255.3, "ref": 223.8, "first_hz": 263.7, "takes": 3}, "words_key": "generation/v2/d83940b7-7327-4e94-8ed9-b64f2d40f63b/audio/d917c7e8441dbf81.words.json", "element": {}}}, {"id": "2e84c6fd", "narration": "Genau! Das Meer ist salzig, weil Salz ankommt und bleibt. Tsch\u00fcss, bis zum n\u00e4chsten Mal!", "scene": {"type": "presenter", "props": {"character": "bear", "side": "left", "framing": "auto", "heading": "Tsch\u00fcss!", "backdrop": "tall_lighthouse_cliff", "cast": ["fox", "bear", "owl"]}}, "speaker": "bear", "translation": "Exactly! The sea is salty because salt arrives and stays. Goodbye, until next time!", "media": {"tts_hash": "6f93dcc44843aaf3", "audio_key": "generation/v2/d83940b7-7327-4e94-8ed9-b64f2d40f63b/audio/6f93dcc44843aaf3.wav", "duration": 5.032, "voice": "Lennart", "register": {"hz": 95.2, "ref": 109.3, "first_hz": 95.2, "takes": 3}, "words_key": "generation/v2/d83940b7-7327-4e94-8ed9-b64f2d40f63b/audio/6f93dcc44843aaf3.words.json", "element": {}}}], "region": "GB", "vector": {"decision": "offered", "style": "cartoon", "reason": "style_cartoon", "share": 0.2, "candidates": ["tall_lighthouse_cliff", "tall_waterfall_forest", "tall_ocean_lighthouse_night", "tall_space_vertical", "tall_sunset_beach_vertical", "tall_snow_peak_vertical"], "aspect": "9:16", "judged": {"fit": true, "kind": "kids", "why": "Animal characters explaining a simple natural-world idea to children", "scene": "cartoon sea coastline with rocks"}, "used": [], "beats": 8, "cap": 1, "backdrops": ["tall_lighthouse_cliff"]}, "whiteboard": {"decision": "no", "reason": "direction:conversation", "asked": false}, "presenter": {"decision": "presenter", "rea